course: dictionary
lesson: 3270
title: Finding meaning from context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An eraser is a small piece of rubber or plastic that removes pencil marks. You can work this out from the words around it: «An eraser is rubber or plastic mixed with a gritty powder; rubbing picks up the graphite and the eraser crumbles away with it.» The clues are rubbing, graphite (the grey mark on your paper) and crumbles away, so an eraser must be something you rub to lift marks off paper.
explain: Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. Does «rubbing the eraser picks up the pencil mark» still make sense? It does, so your meaning is probably right.
explain: Erasers have a second meaning too. In class, a board eraser is a pad used to wipe a chalkboard or whiteboard clean. The word is the same, but the job is different, so the words around it tell you which meaning the writer means.
fact: An eraser is a small piece of rubber or plastic that removes pencil marks.
fact: A board eraser is a pad used to wipe a chalkboard or whiteboard clean.
fact: An eraser is rubber or plastic mixed with a gritty powder.
fact: Before erasers, people rubbed out pencil with bread.
fact: In French, «une gomme» means eraser, and «un chewing-gum» means chewing gum.
exercise: «An eraser is rubber or plastic mixed with a gritty powder.» What is an eraser made of? | Glass and metal | *Rubber or plastic mixed with a gritty powder | Wood and paper | Water and sugar
exercise: «Rubbing picks up the graphite and the eraser crumbles away with it.» What does an eraser remove? | Crumbs from a sandwich | Paint from a wall | *Pencil marks
exercise: «une gomme» is French. What does it mean in English? | A rubber band | *Eraser | Chewing gum | A pencil case
test: What is a board eraser used for? | Sharpening a pencil | *Wiping a chalkboard or whiteboard clean | Holding papers together | Drawing pictures on paper
test: Why does the eraser crumble away? | It is painted with ink | It is frozen solid | It is soaked in water | *It is rubbed, and it picks up the graphite
exam: Which words in «rubbing picks up the graphite and the eraser crumbles away» are the best clue to what eraser means? | Steep and slope | *Rubbing and graphite | Gravity and friction | Chewing gum
